# Transaction Integrity

When transaction implementation is authorized:

## Required

- Explicit transaction lifecycle per applicable FROZEN ADR / domain spec (ADR-007 when frozen)
- Explicit, allowed state transitions only
- Idempotency for externally repeatable operations
- Safe retry semantics (no duplicate financial effects)
- Atomicity where the domain requires it
- Clear failure handling and exceptional states
- No accidental duplicate charging
- No accidental duplicate settlement
- No ambiguous ownership of financial state

## Prohibited

- Inventing transaction states that conflict with the applicable specification
- Treating webhook/provider events as unquestioned truth without verification rules
- Completing settlement solely because an internal flag changed when external verification is required

## OPEN lifecycle

Until ADR-007 is FROZEN, do not silently invent the canonical state machine in code. Propose ADR / wait for authorization.
